Spring Boot 3.4 and newer including 4.x + Thymeleaf. Needs the nonce CSP from the headers recipe (the request attribute `cspNonce`, written by CspNonceFilter). Nothing loads before a choice; Accept and Reject are equal buttons in the first layer; "Cookie settings" reopens the choice. Put the Google tag ID in consent.js. In the project config list `consent` (and JSESSIONID / XSRF cookies if you use them) in essentialCookies. The consent cookie is written by JavaScript, so it never needs Spring.
