Spring Boot 3.4 and newer including 4.x + Thymeleaf. Boot maps every error to /error and picks the template by status: templates/error/404.html, 410.html, then the series masks 4xx.html and 5xx.html (exact code wins over the mask). Throw ResponseStatusException (or call response.sendError) from the controller BEFORE any output is written, so the status is real; never return a view for a missing record. Keep the shared header/footer fragment free of database queries and session reads (an error page that throws is a second error). Do not leave include-stacktrace/include-message on `always` or `on_param` in production (SEC-007); Boot 4 renames the server.error.* properties to spring.web.error.* and deprecates the old names, so the file below sets both (the names of the other major are ignored). Verify with `curl -i -H 'Accept: text/html'` against the packaged jar (without that header Boot answers errors as JSON): unknown URL 404, /old-page 410, database down 503.
